$A_{2} P-A_{1} P=\frac{\lambda}{2} \quad$ (Condition of minima)



$$
\sqrt{\mathrm{D}^{2}+\mathrm{a}^{2}}-\mathrm{D}=\frac{\lambda}{2}
$$



$$
\begin{aligned}
& \mathrm{D}\left(1+\frac{\mathrm{a}^{2}}{\mathrm{D}^{2}}\right)^{1 / 2}-\mathrm{D}=\frac{\lambda}{2} \\\\
& \mathrm{D}\left(1+\frac{1}{2} \times \frac{\mathrm{a}^{2}}{\mathrm{D}^{2}}\right)-\mathrm{D}=\frac{\lambda}{2} \\\\
& \frac{\mathrm{a}^{2}}{2 \mathrm{D}}=\frac{\lambda}{2} \Rightarrow \mathrm{a}=\sqrt{\lambda \cdot \mathrm{D}} \\\\
& =\sqrt{800 \times 10^{-6} \times 50}
\end{aligned}
$$



$\mathrm{a}=0.2 \mathrm{~mm}$
